; Entity handler: sprite moving sideways at a constant speed (flames of the Pestilent Beast, actors of the ending)
;
; Drives the objects that only slide along x and are drawn from a block with the shift pairs (#R$AC9F): the two flames
; that run along the ledge of room 10 after the Beast has breathed (templates #R$BD22, moving left, and #R$BD34, moving
; right; spawned by #R$B8C5; they kill the monk on contact, observed: the hit flag is set when the monk stands on the
; ledge), and the actors of the ending (the monk of the first scene, #R$BD80, the three flames of the pyre, #R$BDA4,
; and the four crusaders, #R$BDB6 and #R$BDC8: speed 0 and limit 0, so they only animate). Slot (template slot, see
; #R$B6E6): +2 word x speed (signed 8.8; $FFC0 = -0.25 moving left, $0040 moving right), +4 byte x limit (high byte of x
; at which the object is removed: $18 for the left flame, $70 for the right flame, 0 for the actors) and +5 byte not
; used, +6 word x and +8 word y (8.8, high bytes in 2-pixel units), +$A word hit box offset (y, x), +$C word hit box far corner
; (y, x), +$E pointer to the sprite block (#R$9595, #R$959D, #R$95AD ...: attribute, pointer to the shift pairs,
; height, then one graphics address per frame), +$10 byte animation counter and +$11 its reload, +$12 byte frame and
; +$13 number of frames.
; .
; Each frame the speed is added to x; when the high byte of x equals the limit the slot is freed through #R$B426 (SP
; back to slot+2, handler word cleared). Otherwise the position becomes the draw command's (y, x/4), A' = x for the shift
; phase, the hit box is tested against the monk (#R$A851) and the code goes on at #R$B9CF.
;
; SP Slot address + 2 (the handler word was popped by the RET that entered the routine)
@label=UpdateMovingSprite
c$B9B0 POP BC        ; x speed
 $B9B1 POP DE        ; E x limit
; Also entered from the pyre monk (#R$B97D) with BC = 0 and DE = 0, SP at slot+4.
@label=UpdateMovingSprite_Move
*$B9B2 POP HL        ; x word
 $B9B3 ADD HL,BC     ; x moves
 $B9B4 PUSH HL       ; store x
 $B9B5 POP HL        ;
 $B9B6 LD A,H        ; x in 2-pixel units
 $B9B7 CP E          ; at the limit?
 $B9B8 JP Z,$B426    ; yes: free the slot
 $B9BB LD D,H        ; D = x
 $B9BC POP HL        ; y word
 $B9BD LD E,H        ; E = y
